From b1f18f7327701015d350cd80dd6ecb601c185db5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:01:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(update): fetch upstream and build the fork merge
 before pausing gateways

`hermes update` on a fork kept this install's gateways paused through the
whole upstream sync: a network `git fetch upstream` (77 s on worker-6's
blob:none clone), the comparison, and on updates.fork_merge_upstream the
off-tree merge-tree, its conflict card (up to 60 s in a fresh interpreter)
and the CI gate. None of that writes a file of the live checkout. Worker-6's
pause lasted 111 s (incident b111bb8f) against 8-47 s fleet-wide.

`_prepare_upstream_sync` now runs that work in `_cmd_update_impl` after the
origin fetch and the pre-commit-point refusals, before the commit point stops
the gateways. The fork merge is built on origin/main, where the origin pull
leaves a HEAD that is behind or at it; when HEAD has commits origin/main
lacks, the merge is still built on HEAD in the sync as before. The paused
`_sync_with_upstream_if_needed` takes the prepared plan once (same root) and
reuses the merge only when HEAD is the commit it was built on; otherwise it
builds it on HEAD. It never fetches again. The upstream fast-forward, a real
tree move, stays paused under `checkout_move` with its marker, debt and
syntax preflight unchanged. Direct callers with no prepared plan behave as
before.

Behaviour notes: the conflict report and the CI gate now run from the
pre-update checkout's code (the update has not moved the tree yet), and an
update that the pause later defers has already fetched upstream and filed or
staged its merge. `_push_synced_fork` (publish after the upstream ff, the
strictly-behind path only) still runs paused; unchanged here.

Proof: tests/hermes_cli/test_update_upstream_before_pause.py records call
order over a real `cmd_update` on local git fixtures (no network). On base
source all 7 fail: fetch upstream, conflict report and CI gate run after
'pause'. With the change they pass: on the fork-merge path they run before
the pause, the only paused git step is the origin ff, and on the ff path the
upstream `merge --ff-only` runs paused inside a checkout_move bound to the
upstream commit. Mutants (drop the HEAD-ancestor guard, the merge_head
check, the root check, the per-attempt reset, the take-once) each fail one
or more tests. 213 update-related test files: 4459 passed, 0 failed.
